{"uid":"b4c14f2b7938e728","name":"test_a_report_with_no_reason_is_a_contract_violation_with_the_move_still_refused","fullName":"tests.test_unsatisfiable_criteria#test_a_report_with_no_reason_is_a_contract_violation_with_the_move_still_refused","historyId":"be4dce40b00bb88e9f58d5e53bf81207","time":{"start":1791938076959,"stop":1791938076997,"duration":38},"description":"v0.13 task 005 (#92 site 3) strengthens this. The OLD claim, pinned\n    here before the cutover, was: `assert state == \"aborted\"` -- a single\n    reported illegal move was fatal on the FIRST offence, with no re-ask\n    and no ladder at all, and the run ended loudly with a \"contract\n    violation\" log message.\n\n    The NEW claim keeps the old one's real content -- the illegal move is\n    still refused, the task record is still untouched -- and adds what the\n    old assertion could not see: the errors were carried back to the SAME\n    worker verbatim on each re-ask, the ladder ran the FULL\n    `contract_retry_max + 1` attempts through\n    `contract_enforcement.enforce_contract` (the report check as its\n    `extra_validate`) -- the EXACT SAME retry loop `_step_generic_hat`'s\n    sites 1/2 (tasks 003/004) already use for the OTHER four hats' own\n    schema/semantic refusals -- and the outcome is an agent-fault\n    iteration that continues per the table\n    (`T(\"worker\", \"no_verdict_yet\")`) rather than aborting: `_step_worker`'s\n    own `while self.budget_left():` loop, not the ladder, decides when this\n    run ends, and it NEVER sets `self._abort_reason` for an exhausted\n    ladder -- with the run's own iteration budget already spent by the one\n    charged attempt below (`iterations=1`), the run ends `\"failed\"`\n    (unverified, no abort) via the ordinary tail, not `\"aborted\"`.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>v0.13 task 005 (#92 site 3) strengthens this. The OLD claim, pinned<br />\nhere before the cutover, was: <code>assert state == &quot;aborted&quot;</code> -- a single<br />\nreported illegal move was fatal on the FIRST offence, with no re-ask<br />\nand no ladder at all, and the run ended loudly with a &quot;contract<br />\nviolation&quot; log message.</p>\n<pre><code>The NEW claim keeps the old one's real content -- the illegal move is\nstill refused, the task record is still untouched -- and adds what the\nold assertion could not see: the errors were carried back to the SAME\nworker verbatim on each re-ask, the ladder ran the FULL\n`contract_retry_max + 1` attempts through\n`contract_enforcement.enforce_contract` (the report check as its\n`extra_validate`) -- the EXACT SAME retry loop `_step_generic_hat`'s\nsites 1/2 (tasks 003/004) already use for the OTHER four hats' own\nschema/semantic refusals -- and the outcome is an agent-fault\niteration that continues per the table\n(`T(&quot;worker&quot;, &quot;no_verdict_yet&quot;)`) rather than aborting: `_step_worker`'s\nown `while self.budget_left():` loop, not the ladder, decides when this\nrun ends, and it NEVER sets `self._abort_reason` for an exhausted\nladder -- with the run's own iteration budget already spent by the one\ncharged attempt below (`iterations=1`), the run ends `&quot;failed&quot;`\n(unverified, no abort) via the ordinary tail, not `&quot;aborted&quot;`.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791937657212,"stop":1791937657213,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791937657213,"stop":1791937657213,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"star